# What REMN needs, as ranges. backend/requirements.txt is this file resolved to exact versions with
# hashes, for every platform, and is what an install reads: tools/lock_requirements.sh writes it.
# An upper bound is the next major (the next minor for 0.x packages that break on minors); raising
# one is a change to test, not a routine bump. The file is not named *.in on purpose: Dependabot
# would then re-resolve the lock for Linux alone and drop the packages only Windows needs.
